From 1c1f42ea0da89fe4787340b3dacc5733a3eca4c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:11:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(security): require authentication on all cockpit API
 routes

The cockpit BFF served every /api/v1 route without any authentication while
binding 0.0.0.0. POST /api/v1/resources/apply pipes its body into
kubectl apply using the node kubeconfig, which runs as system:admin in
system:masters, so any host with network reach to a Nexus node could apply
arbitrary manifests and take over the cluster. POST /api/v1/networking/ovs
could likewise rewrite the node's network fabric.

- Add cockpit_auth.py: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (600k iterations) credential
  store, in-memory bearer sessions with TTL, and per-user lockout after
  10 failures in 5 minutes.
- Gate every /api/v1 route behind a valid session except auth/login and
  auth/session; refuse to start if the credential store cannot init.
- Generate a random initial password instead of shipping admin/admin, and
  flag it for rotation. Add POST /api/v1/auth/password, which revokes all
  sessions so a leaked token cannot outlive a credential change.
- Redirect the plaintext port to HTTPS when certs exist so session tokens
  do not travel in the clear; require TLS 1.2+.
- Set HttpOnly/SameSite=Strict cookies, Secure under TLS.
